oj}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0191bf99f350569c02564f218863b112cfa48fefd833f503e483d8963030b0e3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:400499d142fe38f2fd585ca9650a99b1db992f593715a2258f01fad128756699", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nWe are going to use Lemma <REF_0001>\nto glue the sheaves of <MATH_0001>-graded algebras\n<MATH_0002>\nfor <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004> affine open\nover the scheme <MATH_0005>.\nWe have constructed the data necessary for this in\nLemma <REF_0002> and we have checked condition (d) of\nLemma <REF_0003> in\nLemma <REF_0004>. Hence we get the\nsheaf of <MATH_0006>-graded\n<MATH_0007>-algebras\n<MATH_0008>\ntogether with the isomorphisms <MATH_0009> for all\n<MATH_0010> affine open and all <MATH_0011>.\nFor every affine open <MATH_0012> with <MATH_0013> we have a map\n<MATH_0014>.\nHence the map <MATH_0015> exists by functoriality\nof relative glueing, see Remark <REF_0005>.\nThe diagram of the lemma commutes by construction.\nThis characterizes the sheaf of <MATH_0016>-graded\n<MATH_0017>-algebras\n<MATH_0018>\nbecause the proof of Lemma <REF_0006> shows that\nhaving these diagrams commute uniquely determines the maps <MATH_0019>.\nSome details omitted.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d407166ec953b9f0b83a1ad93c3e86d39b9899c265d09b2a007822f9cc708e44", "unit_id": "inventory:constructions:01NR:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:d670ea13edb748053819403e057b99cd2993476d8e857dca7a2d48f034379479", "hash": "sha256:d670ea13edb748053819403e057b99cd2993476d8e857dca7a2d48f034379479", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 128181, "byte_start": 127257, "file": "constructions.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:655eaafd47eb941843d7cba8f775f45baa6f8ae35b92a765471717b713460a52", "line_end": 3580, "line_start": 3563}, "owner_tag": "01NS", "parent_tag": "01NS", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01NS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A} = \\bigoplus_{d \\geq 0} \\mathcal{A}_d$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\text{Proj}$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\mathcal{A}) \\longrightarrow S\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$\\text{Proj}(A)$", "MATH_0008": "$A = \\Gamma(U, \\mathcal{A})$", "MATH_0009": "$U \\subset S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{situation-relative-proj}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{section-spec}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{section-relative-proj-via-glueing}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2bd5560f9a2cb533210f1c0717f87214554340a929c457fc3325532a5e4c441b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:115493d3c0496f59eaf77914d3ed1e853f90fdd850bcd83ef21134a8520bfce0", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nWe place ourselves in Situation <REF_0001>.\nSo <MATH_0001> is a scheme and <MATH_0002>\nis a quasi-coherent graded <MATH_0003>-algebra.\nIn this section we relativize the construction of\n<MATH_0004> by constructing a functor which the relative\nhomogeneous spectrum will represent.\nAs a result we will construct a morphism of schemes\n<MATH_0005>\nwhich above affine opens of <MATH_0006> will look like the homogeneous spectrum\nof a graded ring. The discussion will be modeled after our\ndiscussion of the relative spectrum in Section <REF_0002>.\nThe easier method using glueing schemes of the form\n<MATH_0007>, <MATH_0008>, <MATH_0009>\naffine open, is explained in Section <REF_0003>,\nand the result in this section will be shown to be isomorphic to that one.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b9644096422aa68e5bfcf52